!?TL0&58;
!!SN:Ev65/1/?y1/?y2/?y3/?y4; call MouseGet(x,y,lmb,rmb)
;!IF:L^DBG: x: %Y1, y: %Y2, center HD: 832x517, center SD: 295x269^;
; 2*x center: for 1920x1080 resolution, axb source size in HD mod it's 1665 (each tile is 45 px, center of first tile on the left is at 22 or 23 px)
; 2*x center for original 800x600 resolution: 591
; Assuming 1920x1080 screen resolution, 1365x768 source size in HD mod, HD version of XFiles.dll from 
!!VRy1:-560; cancel offset from MouseGet in HD XFiles.dll
!!VRy1&y1<0:S0;
!!VRy2:-229; cancel offset from MouseGet in HD
!!VRy2&y2<0:S0;
!!VRy5:Sy1*2-1665*y5; (2dx)^2
;!VRy5:Sy1-832*y5; (dx)^2
; 2*y center for 1920x1080 res is 1035, for 800x600 it's 539
!!VRy6:Sy2*2-1035*y6; (2dy)^2
;!VRy6:Sy2-517*y6; (dy)^2
!!VRy7:Sy5+y6;
; check if 3.5 or more tiles away, 1 tile is 32 px on 800x600 resolution, assume 1920x1080 with 45 pixel tiles
; for 1920x1080 res: (2*45*3.5)^2-1=99224
; for 800x600 res: (2*32*3.5)^2-1=50175
;!IF:L^dbg: dx2: %Y5, dy2: %Y6, 2sqdist: %Y7/99224^;
!!if&y7>99224; 
;!if&y7>24806; 
; MousePut(x,y)--move mouse pointer to center (assume 1920x1080 screen resolution, so 832/517 is the correct destination; it's 296/270 for 800x600)
; Okay, here's the math.
; Assumptions:
; 1920x1080 screen resolution,
; 1365x768 source size in HD mod, 32-bit stretchable mode (tested on HD mod 4.202RC5, bilinear shrapnel x2 filter)
; XFiles.dll used is the one from JV's box.com folder, the one mentioned in file "XFiles for HD Mod-README.txt"
; Calculations:
; Actual X I want: 832 (because it's 18.5 tiles from the left edge, each tile 45 px wide)
; MouseGet returns this with an offset of (1920-800)/2=560
; So virtual X that I want: 832+560=1392
; MousePut does that, but takes arguments offset by 1920-800-1120
; So I need to pass an X of 1392-1120=272 to MousePut in order to land the cursor at the center of the hero.
; Actual Y that I want: 517 (because it's 11.5 tiles from the top edge, each tile 45 px high)
; MouseGet returns that with an offset of (1080-622)/2=229
; So virtual Y that I want is 517+229=746
; MousePut does that, but takes arguments offset by 1080-622=458
; So I need to pass a Y of 746-458=288 to MousePut in order to land the cursor at the center of the hero.
  !!SN:Ev41/1/272/288;
!!en;
; (can't check y3=0 here, spell click not cleared)

